ompleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.4-stable\n\n### System information\n\nDebian GNU/Linux 12.9 (Gnome 43.9)\n\n### Issue description\n\nAfter switching from fullscreen to windowed mode, the window moves up, and sometimes to the top left, and calling `move_to_center` right after does nothing.\n\nI'm not sure if the bug is that the window moves when switching, that `move_to_center` happens without waiting for the window switch, that something's missing in the documentation, or any of these at once.\n\nIdeally, switching modes shouldn't move the window, and `move_to_center` should wait or get queued until the window is ready.\n\nPutting a wait between the switch and `move_to_center` does work, but how much do I need to wait? Is there any way to know that the window is ready?\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nRun the following code:\n\n```gdscript\nget_window().set_mode(Window.MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN)\nawait get_tree().create_timer(1).timeout\nget_window().set_mode(Window.MODE_WINDOWED)\nget_window().move_to_center()\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/use